cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Sentinel XAI: Evidence-Grounded and Agreement-Aware Explainable Network Intrusion Detection with Controlled LLM-Assisted Reporting"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >
  Sentinel XAI is an explainable network intrusion detection system based
  on CICIDS2018 with a strict separation between deterministic security
  evidence and natural-language presentation. A Random Forest classifier
  operates on 30 selected flow features after training-only feature
  selection. SHAP and LIME explain the same local flow, and their
  normalized top-10 feature sets are compared using Jaccard similarity.
  A bounded local SmolLM2 layer is used only for readability, while
  prediction, confidence, SHAP evidence, Jaccard value, and review wording
  remain deterministic. Generated bridge phrases are checked against an
  evidence contract and can be replaced by deterministic fallback.
keywords:
  - "Network intrusion detection"
  - "Explainable AI"
  - "SHAP"
  - "LIME"
  - "Random Forest"
  - "Jaccard similarity"
  - "large language models"
  - "SmolLM2"
  - "CICIDS2018"
  - "evidence-grounded explanation"
